fle rules in effect now this  isn't really explained fully in the show  but the riffle rule is what disables an  adult's ability to directly see magic  the purpose of the rule was to  prevent adults from discovering using or  abusing the powers of the keys I'm  hoping we'll get a little more clarity  on this next season  now the keepers of the keys end up  giving them up vowing never to use them  except for Ellie whose life had taken a  downward toll with the death of her high  school sweetheart Lucas still weighing  heavily on her other people lives get  bigger for I felt like that was just a  Pyrrhic she hit her breaking point and  ventured to the well house using the  echo key to summon Lucas from the dead  but it's not really Lucas it's actually  the demon will come to know as dodge you  may have missed it but the show explains  the origins of the name dodge as a  nickname given to Lucas at school he was  a star fencer with a tremendous ability  to dodge and parry attacks so Ellie gave  him that nickname  Ellie could sense this wasn't the real  Lucas and was like hey great seeing you  and go some harder than the girls that  match me on tinder you see an echo can  only escape the well house by using the  anywhere key a key which allows its  wielder to travel through any door in  the world as long as they've seen it  before  when bodis mother gets stuck in the  mirror he comes running for dodges help  who subsequently tricks him and steals  the keys so she can chow down and steal  expensive jewelry by the way  edan eating a ton of food in the final  scene is a fun callback to episode 2  gaben Eden's demonic brunch wouldn't  have been possible without Dodge  completely foiling the locks family plan  to stop Dodge for good in fact at the  end of the season the lock family still  thinks everything is back to normal they  even decide to stay in Massachusetts  rather than pack up their things and  venture back to Seattle  by the way hate to break it to you guys  but this isn't actually Massachusetts  the show was shot in Nova Scotia and  Ontario fun things story fact I actually  went to school here not Matheson Academy  it's actually a college in Canada  in the novel's the story is set in  Lovecraft Massachusetts named after the  horror fiction writer HP Lovecraft but  it was author Joe Hill's idea to change  it to Matheson after Richard Matheson  the author of I am Legend some of you  may know author Joe Hill but may not  know he's the son of Stephen King and  even makes a guest appearance as a  paramedic in the final episode the show  is actually filled with cameos like  legendary prosthetic artist Tom Savini  who Scott Cavendish and his friends  named their friend group after but back  to the main dilemma that goes like dodge  cannot be killed I mean we literally  can't kill her ELISA decos can't be  killed by normal means so the gang  decides to trap it back where it came  from  the black door but dodge has her own  plans and she's armed with what's known  in the novels as the shadow crown when  it's combined with the shadow key  it essentially activates giving the  wielder the ability to control the  shadows we see this with dodges attack  on the lock house whose shadows are in  search of the Omega key the Omega key is  arguably one of the most important keys  and was the first to be made by Benjamin  Locke a great great ancestor of Tyler  Kinsey and bode way back in 1775 it's so  important in fact that Rendell Locke  buries it in his skull so no one can get  to it a fact that's only made known to  his family when Nina goes full crazy and  smashes the jar of ashes revealing these  still intact key  Benjamin Locke found the black door  while hiding during the American  Revolution accidentally letting the  children of laying escape the children  of laying are the demons whose world is  only accessible through that black door  in order to survive however they need a  human host demons who fail to find a  host turn into what's called whispering  iron although the show never mentions it  this is likely an example of it shown  here this iron is the same material that  the keys are made out of with bori  disintegrating dodges shadow with the  matchstick key the gang is led to  believe this body here is dodges but  this is all part of a greater master  plan we find out that dodge used the  identity key on Ellie turning her into  an identical copy of dodge so while the  gang thought they were throwing dodge  through the black door it was actually  Ellie who  the real world is simply considered a  missing person that really really sucks  but not as bad as Rufus who now has to  live with his uncle in Nebraska and hold  on a second can we just acknowledge how  much of a player dodges demon just  straight-up made up with Kinzie then two  seconds later uses the anywhere key and  makes out with her brother and don't  even get me started on this whole  polyamory storyline no thank you  so the family finally decides to let  Rendell's ashes go Nina had previously  kept the urn above the fireplace but  scattering the ashes over the cliffs is  symbolic of her in the family moving on  with their lives  Randall's death was the catalyst for  many of our characters weaknesses that  we had to see them overcome Kinzie for  example believes that she's a coward  when Sam lesser the team who killed her  father confronted her at gunpoint she  had the chance to try and attack him  with a fire poker but she was too afraid  to do it she's even afraid to go on a  date with Scott but by the end of the  season she's killed her own fear  literally and is open to dating multiple  people at the same time talk about a  change then there's Tyler who's haunted  by the death of his father he believes  that it's his fault Randall died in a  conversation with Sam he vents his  frustrations saying you ever do decide  to kill your dad and do me a favor  kill mine while you're at it it's four  episodes later that Tyler finds out his  words had nothing to do with Rendell's  death Sam killed Rendell because he was  being manipulated by dodge it had  nothing to do with what Tyler had said  this guilt weighs heavily on Tyler  throughout the season causing him to be  overprotective of those he loves to make  up for it when confronting an [ __ ]  hitting on his sister he wastes no time  beating the crap out of him this is  further personified when for a brief  moment the player turns into Sam with  their characters having changed and  everything hunky-dory all seems right in  the world until the revelation that  dodge had been secretly undercover as  Gabe via the identity key he also  happens to be the only one who witnessed  Eden get hit by one of those demonic  bullets this leads us with tons of  theories of where the show might be  headed with two demons on the loose and  both of them under cover a lot of damage  can be done now we know the Locke family  is in possession of several of the keys  as seen here and most importantly the  Omega key it's highly likely that Eden  and Gabe will use the element of  surprise to their advantage to gain  control of more of these keys and with  Scott essentially having cut ties with  Kinsley romantically that leaves our  undercover Gabe the perfect opportunity  to exploit his love with Kinsley in  order to access her box  I mean her musical box we also have the  relationship between Tyler and Jackie  now we know Jackie considers herself a  history buff and Anglophile heck Tyler  even throws a book about British history  in his head to learn more to impress her  and I think this could lead to Jackie  and Tyler looking more into the history  of the Locke family after all the event  which started the families entanglement  with the keys all centered around the  American Revolution against the British  we've only had a brief glimpse of the  ghost of Chamberlain Locke who roams the  graveyard on the lock estate but we  didn't get to learn at all about  Benjamin the original creator of the  keys I wouldn't be surprised if season  two delves more into the origins of the  keys not to mention a slew of keys that  are known in the books but haven't yet  been introduced in the show one such  important key is the Alpha key the only  object that can separate a demon from  the human soul that might sound like  good news for Eden but the process of  removing a demon from its human soul  results in the death of both now you  might think one I just used a head key  to travel into the brain and just remove  the demon that way  well since the demon latches onto your  soul and not your mind it simply doesn't  work that way  in the books the Alpha key is created by  Tyler so it's possible we could see him  creating new keys to combat Gabe and  Eden in season 2 now the show only  really covered about ten keys give or  take but throughout the graphic novels  there are roughly thirty four if you're  interested in learning more about these  keys I've left a link to the lock and  key wiki page in the description below  and we'll le come back well with Rufus  shipped off to Nebraska and the Locke  family really getting over quite quickly  I'd probably guess no le story and the  novel's is drastically different she  doesn't even get sucked into the black  door at all so unfortunately that  doesn't give us any clues it's still  uncertain whether lock and key will be  back for another season but with its big  cliffhanger and the growing popularity  of these haunted house type shows I'd be  surprised if it didn't come back  around 2:00 I hope you all enjoyed this  video please like and subscribe and tell  me in the comments below what you  thought of the show you can also reach  out and follow me on twitter @ think  story YT as the best way to stay in  touch until next time remember  [Music]

